      <p>OpenShift Container Platform administrators can use container compute resource requests and limits to allow and manage the overcommitment of resources on a node, which enables pods to use additional resources when available, without guaranteeing those resources.</p>
      <p>In an <em>overcommited</em> state, the sum of the container compute resource requests and limits exceeds the resources available on the system. Overcommitment might be desirable in development environments where a trade-off of guaranteed performance for capacity is acceptable.</p>
